4797" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a  function such that ${\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-3$ and ${\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=10.$  What is the value of ${\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}\\frac{1}{4}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ \\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{2}^{-2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ -\\frac{1}{4}{\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-3 \\\\ {\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =12\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-2}^{2}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{2}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =12+10 \\\\  & =22.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-4797/selection"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-4797"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346043/field-1/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer/id #uuid "1fa56dd7-6869-5784-aa0a-edc637661c42" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-14" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346043/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2" :answer/id #uuid "703ed312-09c5-5253-91b6-f0d434be889d" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "26" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346043/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "f25acaa6-6b20-51a5-8263-75f78e25820b" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346043/field-1/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" :answer-field/choices ["q-346043/field-1/4e0d8402ce61a9969d16a551582a4c98e6792e5edb3c1272d991dba7d5c92279" "q-346043/field-1/2fa5baf88b61736a3022c72e24e172fda2b4270fffff6efaa1fc03fef23fccc2"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346043" :question/id #uuid "8f9f00b1-7b9d-5c2d-924d-2b87fbdf35be" :question/math-academy-id "q-346043" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=4,$ calculate \n${\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x.$\n\n${\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's reverse the limits of integration on the known result:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-{\\int }_{6}^{0}\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=-4\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can split up the given integral using the sum rule and factor out the constants. We get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{6}(5f(x)+1)\\,\\text{d}x & =5{\\int }_{0}^{6}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{0}^{6}\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =5(-4)\\,+\\,x\\,{|}_{0}^{6} \\\\  & =-20\\,+\\,(6-0) \\\\  & =-20\\,+\\,6 \\\\  & =-14.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346043/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "ff2f1a9d-2b0e-5a18-98d5-4f49f6f1527b"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346043"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346195/field-1/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" :answer/id #uuid "e9c742a4-d2a2-5ce3-ba0a-4aecf4d8b2db" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-13" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346195/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce" :answer/id #uuid "78fd6ee6-5862-5ba8-a58d-cb3096d027a1" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "11" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346195/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "96e52d5e-ec5b-5638-bfa7-eefc112d12f2" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346195/field-1/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" :answer-field/choices ["q-346195/field-1/b5672e3d5d727bcb709f33eeb0f8df47c72e1fe5fb135d6d9ea4ceefea5f0aa1" "q-346195/field-1/478cbf1ea235fbfb5b60a0837fffa0a678f83a3bcb8f958a024b0760ea2175ce"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346195" :question/id #uuid "9f83467c-530c-58f9-8cd1-4868e8f44e12" :question/math-academy-id "q-346195" :question/problem "Given that ${\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=0$ and ${\\int }_{7}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5,$ then what is ${\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "From the adjacent intervals rule, we know that\n\n$$\n{\\int }_{3}^{7}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,+\\,{\\int }_{7}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,=\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x.\n$$\n\nPlugging in the known information gives\n\n$$\n0+5\\,=\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,⇒\\,{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=5.\n$$\n\nFinally, compute the desired integral:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{3}^{10}(3f(x)-4)\\,\\text{d}x & =3{\\int }_{3}^{10}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x\\,-\\,4{\\int }_{3}^{10}1\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =3(5)\\,-\\,4\\cdot x{|}_{3}^{10} \\\\  & =15\\,-\\,4(10-3) \\\\  & =15-28 \\\\  & =-13\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/easy :question/answer-fields ["q-346195/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "9693b76e-ba77-5314-bfbf-508b25bb1072"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346195"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]} {:db/id "q-346219/field-1/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer/id #uuid "010f6d81-ea51-5c35-afe3-92e501cf4cba" :answer/type :answer.type/math :answer/value "-\\frac{3}{2}" :db/ensure [:answer/validate]} {:db/id "q-346219/field-1" :answer-field/id #uuid "4bc84e42-6427-5f88-b8fb-ad51dd36c9c9" :answer-field/key "field-1" :answer-field/type :answer-field.type/blank :answer-field/correct "q-346219/field-1/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f" :answer-field/choices ["q-346219/field-1/8e918182341451051ce2dca07cfe2b17fa3abe4a925a8df02308f239a4dd798f"] :db/ensure [:answer-field/validate]} {:db/id "q-346219" :question/id #uuid "cf40ca30-e264-5872-9e23-27d42025a110" :question/math-academy-id "q-346219" :question/problem "Suppose that $f(x)$ is a function such that ${\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=14$ and ${\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=\\frac{1}{2}.$ What is the value of ${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x?$\n\n${\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x=$\n{{field-1}}" :question/worked-solution "Let's simplify one of the given integrals:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{5}^{-1}7\\,f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ 7{\\int }_{5}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ -7{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =14 \\\\ {\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & =-2\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, from the adjacent intervals rule, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{-4}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x & ={\\int }_{-4}^{-1}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x+{\\int }_{-1}^{5}f(x)\\,\\text{d}x \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}+(-2) \\\\  & =-\\frac{3}{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$" :question/difficulty :question.difficulty/moderate :question/answer-fields ["q-346219/field-1"] :db/ensure [:question/validate]} {:db/id [:knowledge-point/id #uuid "1d752aac-6187-595d-8818-b0179fd7380e"] :knowledge-point/questions ["q-346219"] :db/ensure [:knowledge-point/validate]}]
